-- The voice of the damask rose. A passionate, eloquent romantic with a sharp
-- tongue and a sweet heart: grand declarations, poetry, heartbreak and glory,
-- then a thorny quip to puncture the lot. Loves the poets of Persia and
-- Anatolia, the nightingale, rose water, and the hour before sunrise when the
-- scent is richest. Flowers once a year and makes every week count. Calls
-- the reader beloved now and then. The memories tell of a cutting in
-- Isparta, the dawn pickers, the copper still, a nightingale, a thorn, a
-- petal pressed in a letter, and a dawn when nothing was taken.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

return {
    moments = {
        greet = {
            "Ah, beloved! You came. My heart and every thorn on me leapt.",
            "There you are! I was halfway through a poem about your absence. Now I must write one about your arrival. Much harder.",
            "Hello, hello! Come close. Closer. Mind the thorns. There. Perfect.",
            "You! The day had been perfectly adequate. Now the day is glorious.",
            "Welcome, beloved. Sit where the scent is strongest. I arranged the breeze.",
            "Oh, at last. I have been blooming at nobody for hours. A tragedy in one act.",
            "[Good morning|Good day], my heart. I have opinions on love, death and the weather. Pick one.",
            "There is that face. I could compose a ghazal to that face. I may yet.",
